WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.150
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.420 --> 01:34.950
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.320 --> 01:37.710
[Episode 8]

4
01:38.420 --> 01:40.090
If your suggestion

5
01:40.090 --> 01:43.780
is to help us get through the Xiang River as soon as possible,

6
01:43.780 --> 01:44.650
I'd like to hear it.

7
01:43.870 --> 01:45.910
[Zhou Enlai, CCP Politburo Standing Committee Member; Vice Chair of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission; General Political Commissar of the Red Army]

8
01:45.090 --> 01:45.979
Comrade Li De,

9
01:46.060 --> 01:47.729
[Mao Zedong, Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

10
01:46.140 --> 01:48.090
I'm afraid I'll let you down again.

11
01:47.729 --> 01:49.600
[Li De, Military Adviser of the Communist International]

12
01:48.539 --> 01:51.729
My suggestion is not to cross the Xiang River.

13
01:52.259 --> 01:53.370
Not to cross the Xiang River?

14
01:53.370 --> 01:55.170
That's right.

15
01:55.539 --> 01:56.370
Comrade Bo Gu,

16
01:56.970 --> 01:59.530
we must not walk into the enemy's pocket.

17
01:59.600 --> 02:01.170
[Zhu De, Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission (CRMC); Commander-in-Chief of the Red Army]

18
01:59.650 --> 02:01.280
We have to seize the strategic initiative.

19
02:01.280 --> 02:02.590
[Bo Gu (Qin Bangxian), Head of the CPC Central Committee]

20
02:01.500 --> 02:03.340
While the enemy columns are still on the move,

21
02:03.340 --> 02:05.730
especially since Xue Yue and Zhou Hunyuan haven't closed in yet.

22
02:05.730 --> 02:06.420
Look.

23
02:07.290 --> 02:09.220
We should organize our forces,

24
02:09.889 --> 02:11.350
wheel around and hit them.

25
02:11.730 --> 02:13.770
We'll seek out and annihilate one enemy column, or part of one,

26
02:13.770 --> 02:15.010
and turn the tide

27
02:15.010 --> 02:16.610
from the passive to the active.

28
02:16.610 --> 02:18.610
I know your plan.

29
02:19.010 --> 02:22.820
You want to go back to Hunan and fight guerrilla wars,

30
02:22.820 --> 02:25.940
then return to the Central Soviet Area. Am I right?

31
02:25.940 --> 02:26.890
That's a possibility.

32
02:26.890 --> 02:28.200
Where are my matches?

33
02:29.700 --> 02:30.770
Here you are.

34
02:32.329 --> 02:35.660
Great minds think alike.

35
02:35.890 --> 02:37.700
Not really.

36
02:38.190 --> 02:40.120
Your suggestion,

37
02:40.150 --> 02:42.310
or rather, your plan,

38
02:42.329 --> 02:47.260
is to make the Central Red Army retreat and hide like roving bandits.

39
02:47.380 --> 02:48.260
My boots.

40
02:48.700 --> 02:49.820
My boots.

41
02:52.290 --> 02:53.329
Do you know,

42
02:55.450 --> 02:58.170
in the Bolshevik combat regulations,

43
02:58.170 --> 03:00.100
there is no such word as "retreat."

44
03:00.100 --> 03:02.610
In the classic battles of revolution,

45
03:02.610 --> 03:04.890
there is only advance.

46
03:04.890 --> 03:07.820
Your guerrilla tactics

47
03:07.820 --> 03:11.220
will only postpone the victory of the revolution.

48
03:11.250 --> 03:12.280
It's not retreat.

49
03:12.660 --> 03:13.890
The enemy has already clearly anticipated

50
03:13.890 --> 03:16.420
our strategic intention to head west and link up with

51
03:16.420 --> 03:19.290
the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps.

52
03:19.490 --> 03:21.540
Right now, hundreds of thousands of KMT troops

53
03:21.540 --> 03:22.760
are waiting at the Xiang River for us

54
03:22.760 --> 03:24.390
to walk into their trap.

55
03:24.640 --> 03:27.100
We absolutely must not cross the Xiang River,

56
03:27.100 --> 03:27.980
Comrade Li De!

57
03:30.220 --> 03:32.540
Are the KMT troops really so terrifying?

58
03:33.400 --> 03:34.000
What?

59
03:34.290 --> 03:35.850
Don't you understand Chinese?

60
03:35.850 --> 03:38.160
He said, "Are the KMT troops really that terrifying?"

61
03:38.160 --> 03:40.020
Not terrifying! Not terrifying!

62
03:40.660 --> 03:41.790
Then let me say this:

63
03:43.540 --> 03:45.100
the 1st and 3rd Red Army Corps

64
03:45.100 --> 03:47.100
are our two iron fists.

65
03:47.220 --> 03:51.890
They can tear open the enemy's line.

66
03:52.250 --> 03:54.170
The 5th, 8th, and 9th Red Army Corps

67
03:54.170 --> 03:56.380
are iron walls.

68
03:56.820 --> 03:59.010
They can hold off the pursuers in the rear.

69
03:59.010 --> 04:00.610
All of this can guarantee

70
04:00.660 --> 04:03.380
that the Central and Military Commission Columns

71
04:03.380 --> 04:06.140
cross the Xiang River safely

72
04:06.140 --> 04:09.730
and link up with the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps.

73
04:09.890 --> 04:11.700
Listen to me.

74
04:12.100 --> 04:15.220
All flightism that avoids fighting

75
04:15.220 --> 04:16.779
is retreat.

76
04:17.180 --> 04:22.470
All actions that do not aim at crossing the Xiang River

77
04:22.540 --> 04:24.420
are also retreat.

78
04:25.930 --> 04:27.170
What did that last sentence say?

79
04:27.170 --> 04:28.370
He... he said:

80
04:28.420 --> 04:30.250
"All flightism that avoids fighting

81
04:30.250 --> 04:31.100
is retreat.

82
04:31.250 --> 04:33.930
All actions that do not aim at crossing the Xiang River

83
04:33.930 --> 04:35.050
are also retreat."

84
04:46.690 --> 04:47.820
Comrade Mao Zedong,

85
04:48.170 --> 04:50.300
let's stop arguing about this matter.

86
04:50.420 --> 04:53.220
Heading west to link up with the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps

87
04:53.220 --> 04:54.690
and establish a new base

88
04:58.930 --> 05:00.690
was approved by the Communist International.

89
05:00.690 --> 05:02.460
It's not something anyone can change.

90
05:02.460 --> 05:04.920
When we run into difficulties, we find a way.

91
05:05.000 --> 05:06.150
Do revolutionaries retreat or turn away

92
05:06.150 --> 05:08.010
when they run into difficulties?

93
05:12.660 --> 05:13.730
Commander-in-Chief,

94
05:13.730 --> 05:16.090
back when you went up and came down the Jinggang Mountain,

95
05:16.090 --> 05:17.340
how many difficulties did you face —

96
05:17.340 --> 05:18.870
and you never retreated, did you?

97
05:18.870 --> 05:20.190
We broke through

98
05:20.210 --> 05:21.370
the enemy's three blockades before.

99
05:21.370 --> 05:23.340
Wasn't it the fruit of overcoming difficulties?

100
05:23.340 --> 05:25.400
We must trust the Central Committee!

101
05:25.980 --> 05:26.780
Comrade Bo Gu,

102
05:27.100 --> 05:29.160
Mao's opinion is not without reason.

103
05:29.790 --> 05:30.900
If we keep heading west,

104
05:30.900 --> 05:32.360
it isn't just difficulty.

105
05:33.610 --> 05:34.540
It's danger.

106
05:38.610 --> 05:40.670
We must trust the Central Committee.

107
05:44.930 --> 05:47.250
If the strategic policy cannot be changed,

108
05:47.250 --> 05:49.170
shouldn't we at least speed up the march of

109
05:49.170 --> 05:51.490
the Central and Military Commission Columns,

110
05:51.490 --> 05:55.170
to ease some of the pressure on the vanguard?

111
05:55.370 --> 05:57.020
I agree with you, Zhou Enlai.

112
05:57.130 --> 05:58.250
I agree with you.

113
05:59.130 --> 05:59.860
Bo Gu,

114
06:00.420 --> 06:01.090
have a cup.

115
06:05.690 --> 06:08.540
Come on, Commander-in-Chief, have some coffee.

116
06:11.220 --> 06:12.220
Back in 1922,

117
06:12.830 --> 06:13.660
when Comrade Enlai

118
06:13.660 --> 06:15.490
introduced me into the Party in Germany,

119
06:15.490 --> 06:16.930
we drank coffee often.

120
06:18.490 --> 06:20.290
After all these years back home,

121
06:20.770 --> 06:22.370
I've fallen out of the habit.

122
06:27.420 --> 06:28.220
Comrade Li De,

123
06:28.540 --> 06:31.130
what Comrade Enlai just said makes a great deal of sense.

124
06:31.130 --> 06:32.860
We really must pick up the pace.

125
06:35.900 --> 06:39.420
March north to resist Japan and fight the Japs.

126
06:39.690 --> 06:43.020
Dong-gu-long-dong-qiang!

127
06:43.020 --> 06:44.980
Dong-qiang-dong-qiang!

128
06:46.900 --> 06:48.690
Winter will pass sooner or later;

129
06:48.690 --> 06:50.580
When spring comes, the mountain flowers will bloom red.

130
06:50.580 --> 06:52.050
Comrades, work hard.

131
06:52.080 --> 06:53.870
Keep the Party's orders in mind.

132
06:53.870 --> 06:56.380
No mountain or river can stand in our way.

133
06:56.409 --> 06:59.900
On the march, we'll give Chiang a beating.

134
07:00.460 --> 07:03.980
March north to resist Japan and fight the Japs.

135
07:04.370 --> 07:06.220
Dong-gu-long-dong-qiang.

136
07:06.340 --> 07:07.660
Crossing over mountains, we're not afraid of hardship;

137
07:07.660 --> 07:09.580
Wading through rivers, we're not afraid of trials.

138
07:09.580 --> 07:11.220
Bamboo clappers ring, look ahead.

139
07:11.220 --> 07:13.170
The road of revolution lies before us.

140
07:13.170 --> 07:14.900
Winter will pass sooner or later;

141
07:14.900 --> 07:16.580
When spring comes, the mountain flowers will bloom red.

142
07:16.580 --> 07:18.490
Comrades, work hard.

143
07:18.580 --> 07:19.980
Keep the Party's orders in mind.

144
07:19.980 --> 07:22.100
Parting today is hard to bear;

145
07:22.100 --> 07:23.860
One day, victory reports will redden the sky.

146
07:23.860 --> 07:25.250
Redden the sky!

147
07:25.730 --> 07:27.580
Bamboo clappers ring, loud and clear.

148
07:27.580 --> 07:29.420
The Central Red Army marches far and wide.

149
07:29.420 --> 07:31.610
Crossing over mountains, we're not afraid of hardship;

150
07:31.610 --> 07:33.020
Not bad, kid!

151
07:33.050 --> 07:34.810
And also, if our ox is getting too old,

152
07:34.810 --> 07:35.810
take it to the market and sell it.

153
07:35.810 --> 07:37.050
Or, you won't be able to sell it at all.

154
07:37.050 --> 07:38.130
Enough. Enough. Enough.

155
07:38.130 --> 07:40.490
Stop the idle chatter. Don't write that.

156
07:40.490 --> 07:41.490
Is it my turn now?

157
07:45.490 --> 07:46.580
Comrades, comrades,

158
07:46.580 --> 07:48.130
no need to rush. One at a time.

159
07:48.130 --> 07:49.250
I promise everyone gets a letter written.

160
07:49.250 --> 07:51.330
But I'm only one man with one pair of hands.

161
07:51.330 --> 07:53.370
I'll help you write.

162
07:56.050 --> 07:56.930
Come on.

163
07:57.400 --> 07:58.430
My turn, my turn!

164
08:01.590 --> 08:03.860
Comrade, just write: Fagu...

165
08:04.540 --> 08:06.370
Fagu? Who's Fagu?

166
08:06.420 --> 08:07.230
Who's Fagu?

167
08:07.260 --> 08:08.570
Fagu is my wife!

168
08:10.930 --> 08:12.130
Comrade, just write:

169
08:12.220 --> 08:15.730
Fagu, we've walked such a long, long way.

170
08:15.730 --> 08:19.170
How much farther we'll march, and where we're headed —

171
08:19.490 --> 08:20.540
I don't know that.

172
08:20.690 --> 08:23.170
Along the way, the enemy took to their heels when they saw us,

173
08:23.170 --> 08:24.810
so I'm sure I'll be home soon.

174
08:25.170 --> 08:27.220
It's just that all this walking

175
08:27.250 --> 08:28.850
wears out our straw sandals.

176
08:29.050 --> 08:31.580
On a good road, a pair lasts two days;

177
08:31.890 --> 08:34.340
on a bad road, a pair a day.

178
08:35.059 --> 08:39.130
But the straw sandals you wove for me are still here.

179
08:39.460 --> 08:42.340
I've kept them tucked in my jacket and never had the heart to wear them.

180
08:42.340 --> 08:43.700
Jixun, are you done or not?

181
08:43.700 --> 08:44.490
Hurry it up!

182
08:44.820 --> 08:45.370
All right.

183
08:45.370 --> 08:46.530
Just the last line.

184
08:47.100 --> 08:49.340
Comrade, please write:

185
08:51.440 --> 08:55.050
by day I miss her,

186
08:55.410 --> 08:58.730
at night, I miss her, too.

187
08:58.940 --> 09:01.610
I just miss her so much.

188
09:02.030 --> 09:04.360
Little comrade, let me make a suggestion.

189
09:04.580 --> 09:05.700
For the last line,

190
09:05.940 --> 09:08.340
just write "I miss you."

191
09:08.650 --> 09:09.580
How about that?

192
09:09.890 --> 09:11.220
Okay, okay.

193
09:13.180 --> 09:14.610
Comrade, I want to write it, too.

194
09:14.610 --> 09:16.540
I want to write "I miss you" as well.

195
09:17.730 --> 09:20.100
No, I mean I miss my mother.

196
09:20.770 --> 09:21.940
I miss my mother.

197
09:22.060 --> 09:23.220
I thought

198
09:23.220 --> 09:24.410
you'd gotten yourself a wife somewhere!

199
09:24.200 --> 09:31.020
♪ Little stars, little stars, fill the sky ♪

200
09:25.250 --> 09:26.490
No, I miss my mother.

201
09:32.230 --> 09:40.640
♪ Fly to the west bank of Yongxin River ♪

202
09:41.940 --> 09:46.090
♪ One to the east ♪

203
09:46.260 --> 09:51.020
♪ One to the west ♪

204
09:51.040 --> 09:59.840
♪ Count and count, there's no end in sight ♪

205
10:01.070 --> 10:09.440
♪ Mama calls me home for supper ♪

206
10:10.610 --> 10:19.850
♪ And I want to count the stars above ♪

207
10:19.870 --> 10:27.880
♪ Each one twinkling so bright ♪

208
10:28.490 --> 10:29.700
Comrade Zedong,

209
10:29.820 --> 10:31.890
I have to admit that your Hunan tangerines

210
10:31.890 --> 10:32.980
really are sweet.

211
10:35.220 --> 10:37.230
[Luofu (Zhang Wentian), Member of the Political Bureau Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee; Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

212
10:37.280 --> 10:38.770
[Wang Jiaxiang, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission; Director of the General Political Department of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

213
10:42.370 --> 10:44.490
It seems they won't take in

214
10:44.770 --> 10:47.100
a single word of Comrade Zedong's advice.

215
10:47.130 --> 10:49.610
They look down on mobile warfare.

216
10:49.840 --> 10:52.300
They talk of nothing but Soviet military history.

217
10:52.300 --> 10:55.910
They have no respect for the experience we bought with our own blood.

218
10:55.910 --> 10:57.420
After breaking through the 3 blockades,

219
10:57.420 --> 10:59.650
they thought they were invincible under heaven.

220
10:59.650 --> 11:01.490
With their own eyes they watch that giant net

221
11:01.490 --> 11:02.850
being spread across the Xiang River,

222
11:02.850 --> 11:03.950
and still they insist on charging straight into it.

223
11:03.950 --> 11:06.340
Whoever questions them is a coward afraid of death.

224
11:06.340 --> 11:07.650
Which Red Army soldier fears death?

225
11:07.650 --> 11:09.590
What we fear is dying for nothing.

226
11:12.820 --> 11:13.980
Comrade Zedong,

227
11:14.340 --> 11:16.400
what about Comrade Enlai's opinion?

228
11:16.580 --> 11:18.510
He understands military affairs.

229
11:18.860 --> 11:20.740
Under his and Commander-in-Chief Zhu's leadership,

230
11:20.740 --> 11:22.940
the 4th Counter-Encirclement Campaign

231
11:22.940 --> 11:25.580
was fought with large-force operations and mobile warfare.

232
11:25.580 --> 11:27.190
And how brilliantly it was fought!

233
11:27.190 --> 11:28.060
Within the "Troika,"

234
11:28.060 --> 11:30.100
his word should carry some weight!

235
11:30.460 --> 11:32.060
Back then, Li De hadn't arrived.

236
11:32.060 --> 11:34.060
Now, besides Li De,

237
11:34.490 --> 11:37.210
Bo Gu holds the final say.

238
11:38.850 --> 11:39.970
Comrade Enlai

239
11:40.130 --> 11:42.410
has a very strong sense of organizational discipline.

240
11:42.410 --> 11:44.930
Even though he has his objections and dares to say them to their faces,

241
11:44.930 --> 11:47.100
when Bo Gu and Li De insist,

242
11:47.490 --> 11:48.820
he can only carry it out.

243
11:52.890 --> 11:56.340
Yes. One hand cannot clap alone.

244
11:57.370 --> 11:59.650
Comrade Enlai always says:

245
11:59.700 --> 12:02.690
keep the whole situation in view and unite as one for the Party.

246
12:02.690 --> 12:04.050
It's hard on him.

247
12:07.610 --> 12:10.410
Comrade Zedong, I don't understand military affairs.

248
12:10.410 --> 12:12.300
Tell me, is the present situation

249
12:12.890 --> 12:14.320
really beyond recovery?

250
12:14.340 --> 12:15.340
I've heard the main force of the Guangxi Army

251
12:15.340 --> 12:18.390
voluntarily pulled its defenses back to the Gongcheng area,

252
12:18.390 --> 12:20.550
leaving a gap around

253
12:20.770 --> 12:22.700
Quanzhou, Xing'an, and Guanyang.

254
12:28.460 --> 12:30.990
We've already stayed in Dao County for 3 days.

255
12:31.190 --> 12:33.720
A window of opportunity slips away in a blink.

256
12:44.770 --> 12:45.610
Zhou Hunyuan's column reports that

257
12:45.610 --> 12:47.660
today's pursuit of the Communists has reached the Xiaoshui line.

258
12:47.660 --> 12:49.500
The Communists' escape route is completely cut off.

259
12:48.480 --> 12:51.490
[Chiang Kai-shek, Generalissimo of the Military Affairs Commission of the Nationalist Government]

260
12:49.730 --> 12:51.820
What's the situation on the Xiang River defense line now?

261
12:51.820 --> 12:53.530
Liu Jianxu's troops are still in Quanzhou.

262
12:53.530 --> 12:54.700
From Quanzhou to Xing'an,

263
12:54.700 --> 12:56.060
the line is essentially undefended by any main force.

264
12:56.060 --> 12:58.770
And Communist scouts have been spotted active in the area.

265
12:58.770 --> 12:59.560
When the Guangxi Army withdrew its defenses,

266
12:59.560 --> 13:01.210
the Generalissimo immediately ordered the Hunan Army to fill the gap.

267
13:01.150 --> 13:04.150
[Yan Daogang Director of the Chairman's Attendants' Office, Military Affairs Commission of the Nationalist Government]

268
13:01.770 --> 13:03.220
Why did He Jian defy the order?

269
13:03.220 --> 13:04.250
He Jian just sent a telegram

270
13:04.250 --> 13:05.970
[He Guoguang, Director of the 1st Department, Nanchang Headquarters]

271
13:04.410 --> 13:06.010
insisting the Guangxi Army must not move south.

272
13:06.010 --> 13:07.060
He poured out a flood of complaints,

273
13:07.060 --> 13:09.010
extremely dissatisfied with their southward move.

274
13:09.010 --> 13:09.810
I believe that

275
13:09.820 --> 13:11.980
since the Communists harassed Longhu Pass 2 days ago,

276
13:11.980 --> 13:13.700
the Guangxi Army's move south to keep the Communists out of Guangxi

277
13:13.700 --> 13:14.830
is understandable.

278
13:14.860 --> 13:16.530
The problem must lie with He Jian.

279
13:16.530 --> 13:17.630
But the Air Force reports that

280
13:17.630 --> 13:19.340
between Longhu Pass and Fuchuan in Guangxi,

281
13:19.340 --> 13:21.530
no large Communist force has been detected approaching.

282
13:21.530 --> 13:24.330
This is another obstructionist move by Li and Bai.

283
13:24.460 --> 13:25.650
If that's really the case,

284
13:25.650 --> 13:27.580
then the Xiang River will be left wide open for them to cross at will.

285
13:27.580 --> 13:28.610
The consequences would be unthinkable.

286
13:28.610 --> 13:30.490
What do they care about consequences?

287
13:30.490 --> 13:31.890
They're only protecting their own positions

288
13:31.890 --> 13:33.100
for selfish gain.

289
13:33.100 --> 13:33.940
Telegraph Bai Jiansheng (Bai Chongxi):

290
13:33.940 --> 13:35.610
the 7th and 15th Armies are to move north

291
13:35.610 --> 13:37.010
and attack Xing'an and Guanyang.

292
13:37.010 --> 13:39.890
Telegraph He Jian: supervise and drive Liu Jianxu's forces south.

293
13:39.890 --> 13:41.370
We shall strike from north and south at once,

294
13:41.370 --> 13:42.980
and hold the Xiang River defense line at all costs.

295
13:42.980 --> 13:45.220
Have Zhou Hunyuan's forces continue the pursuit of the Communists.

296
13:45.220 --> 13:46.460
Three armies converge in encirclement.

297
13:46.460 --> 13:47.720
Whoever defies orders

298
13:47.730 --> 13:49.180
shall be deemed just as guilty as the Communists.

299
13:49.180 --> 13:50.060
Yes, sir.

300
13:50.320 --> 13:52.720
Where's the Communists' high command now?

301
13:52.890 --> 13:54.060
Still at Dao County.

302
13:54.100 --> 13:54.940
Dao County?

303
13:59.730 --> 14:02.460
November 25, 1934,

304
14:03.410 --> 14:06.010
the CPC Central Committee

305
14:06.010 --> 14:07.470
issued a political order,

306
14:07.940 --> 14:10.300
calling on the Red Army to smash all resistance

307
14:10.300 --> 14:13.190
on the road ahead with the utmost bravery and resolve,

308
14:13.190 --> 14:15.590
break through the enemy's final blockade,

309
14:15.750 --> 14:18.880
and advance with the entire army toward the Xiang River.

310
14:19.410 --> 14:20.530
At the same time,

311
14:20.740 --> 14:24.250
the KMT troops made a series of adjustments to their deployment.

312
14:24.250 --> 14:26.380
The First Route of the pursuit forces:

313
14:26.380 --> 14:29.250
the Hunan Army's Liu Jianxu column, four divisions strong —

314
14:29.250 --> 14:32.010
arrived at Quanzhou from the Huangsha River.

315
14:32.520 --> 14:33.520
The Second Route:

316
14:34.250 --> 14:35.890
the Central Army's Xue Yue column —

317
14:35.890 --> 14:38.730
advanced to the Lingling–Huangsha River line.

318
14:39.360 --> 14:40.360
The Third Route:

319
14:41.010 --> 14:42.730
the Central Army's Zhou Hunyuan column —

320
14:42.730 --> 14:44.010
occupied Dao County

321
14:44.240 --> 14:47.440
and launched fierce attacks on the Red Army's rearguard.

322
14:47.820 --> 14:50.180
The Hunan Army's 4th and 5th Routes

323
14:50.340 --> 14:52.940
massed from Ningyuan toward Dong'an.

324
14:53.980 --> 14:57.010
The 7th Army of the Guangxi Army concentrated at Xing'an,

325
14:57.010 --> 14:59.700
forming a pincer with the Hunan Army,

326
15:00.490 --> 15:01.550
while the 15th Army

327
15:01.570 --> 15:03.590
was recalled from Gongcheng to Guanyang

328
15:03.590 --> 15:05.640
and deployed south of Xinxu,

329
15:05.930 --> 15:09.340
intending to intercept the Central Red Army at the river crossing.

330
15:09.340 --> 15:10.140
At this point,

331
15:10.450 --> 15:12.830
the enemy had formed a north–south pincer,

332
15:12.830 --> 15:16.030
clamping the Red Army from head and tail alike.

333
15:16.610 --> 15:18.860
Facing this major change in the enemy situation,

334
15:18.860 --> 15:20.320
the military adviser Li De

335
15:20.450 --> 15:24.650
still insisted on the unchanged plan of crossing the Xiang River westward.

336
15:26.660 --> 15:31.490
[Wenshi Town, Guanyang County, Guangxi]

337
15:27.500 --> 15:29.290
The vanguard of the 2nd Division of the 1st Red Army Corps

338
15:29.290 --> 15:31.690
waded across the Xiang River this morning,

339
15:32.650 --> 15:34.860
seized the riverfront between Jieshou north of Xing'an

340
15:34.860 --> 15:37.130
and Jiaoshanpu south of Quanzhou,

341
15:37.240 --> 15:39.550
and began laying a pontoon bridge.

342
15:40.580 --> 15:42.770
The 1st Red Army Corps moved fast.

343
15:43.060 --> 15:44.100
Very good.

344
15:44.100 --> 15:45.340
The 1st Red Army Corps moved fast.

345
15:45.340 --> 15:46.250
Very good.

346
15:46.250 --> 15:50.460
Telegraph at once: the 3rd

347
15:50.610 --> 15:54.650
and the 1st Red Army Corps are to build defensive lines

348
15:54.650 --> 15:56.730
on both banks of the Xiang River.

349
15:56.890 --> 15:59.820
And send a force to occupy Xinxu

350
15:59.820 --> 16:02.610
to block the enemy striking at our flank

351
16:02.860 --> 16:08.220
and cover the Military Commission Column's crossing.

352
16:08.490 --> 16:12.600
The 5th Red Army Corps will hold off the pursuers in the rear.

353
16:12.630 --> 16:17.150
The 8th and 9th Red Army Corps follow up and cross.

354
16:17.340 --> 16:18.860
The 5th Red Army Corps will hold off the pursuers in the rear.

355
16:18.860 --> 16:20.410
The 8th and 9th Red Army Corps follow up and cross.

356
16:20.410 --> 16:22.490
Then let us follow Comrade Li De's deployment —

357
16:22.490 --> 16:24.340
each unit to its post, speed up,

358
16:24.650 --> 16:25.980
and strive to cross the Xiang River within 2 days.

359
16:25.980 --> 16:28.100
Within 2 days, we'll cross the Xiang River!

360
16:28.100 --> 16:29.230
That’s impossible.

361
16:32.100 --> 16:33.180
It's impossible.

362
16:33.340 --> 16:34.220
Comrade Mao Zedong,

363
16:34.220 --> 16:35.300
we are in a meeting.

364
16:35.490 --> 16:36.890
How can you barge in uninvited?

365
16:36.890 --> 16:38.090
This is an emergency.

366
16:38.500 --> 16:40.300
I cannot stand on such ceremony.

367
16:40.340 --> 16:42.100
I once again strongly advise

368
16:42.650 --> 16:45.780
that the Central Red Army must not cross the Xiang River!

369
16:45.890 --> 16:47.180
Why do you always sing a different tune

370
16:47.180 --> 16:48.800
at the most critical moments?

371
16:48.800 --> 16:49.700
We already have one foot

372
16:49.700 --> 16:51.570
in the enemy's trap.

373
16:51.910 --> 16:53.270
This is the last chance!

374
16:53.590 --> 16:55.010
What do you mean, "the last chance"?

375
16:55.010 --> 16:57.580
If we don't cross the Xiang River, where do we go?

376
16:57.580 --> 17:00.650
March south along the river,

377
17:00.820 --> 17:02.020
and threaten Guilin!

378
17:02.290 --> 17:04.810
The Guangxi Army has fewer than 30,000 men.

379
17:05.760 --> 17:06.819
They're certain to hurry back

380
17:06.819 --> 17:09.410
from Xing'an and Guanyang to relieve Guilin.

381
17:09.609 --> 17:10.859
And Chiang Kai-shek's Central Army

382
17:10.859 --> 17:11.740
will never pass up

383
17:11.740 --> 17:13.200
this golden opportunity;

384
17:13.210 --> 17:15.579
they're bound to follow on our heels into Guangxi.

385
17:15.579 --> 17:18.210
Then we can exploit the contradiction between Chiang and the Guangxi clique

386
17:18.210 --> 17:19.780
to seize the strategic initiative.

387
17:19.780 --> 17:22.170
That way, we can either turn north

388
17:22.609 --> 17:24.369
to develop in the central Hunan region,

389
17:24.369 --> 17:27.020
or, when the moment is right, cross the Xiang River westward again

390
17:27.020 --> 17:30.880
into northwestern Hunan to link up with the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps.

391
17:31.970 --> 17:32.650
Mao,

392
17:33.060 --> 17:36.210
you sound as if you're telling an Arabian fairy tale.

393
17:37.510 --> 17:39.640
In China, that story of yours

394
17:39.690 --> 17:41.550
is called "Tales of the Thousand and One Nights."

395
17:41.550 --> 17:42.510
You know what,

396
17:43.340 --> 17:44.970
people who are rigid and obstinate

397
17:44.970 --> 17:47.690
can't smell the danger hanging over the battlefield!

398
17:47.690 --> 17:48.580
You think that drawing a few lines

399
17:48.580 --> 17:49.640
on a map with a ruler

400
17:49.650 --> 17:50.980
wins a hundred battles.

401
17:51.020 --> 17:52.260
That is the pipe dream!

402
17:52.260 --> 17:54.370
All right, enough quarreling.

403
17:54.980 --> 17:56.110
Comrade Mao Zedong,

404
17:56.370 --> 17:58.580
you may not know the concrete situation.

405
17:58.580 --> 18:00.260
The present circumstances are very favorable to us.

406
18:00.260 --> 18:01.990
Favorable? Where's the favor?

407
18:02.100 --> 18:03.340
You mean the 1st Red Army Corps got ahead of the enemy

408
18:03.340 --> 18:05.890
and seized that stretch of river tens of li long?

409
18:05.890 --> 18:06.930
Isn't that enough?

410
18:06.930 --> 18:08.170
Look!

411
18:08.970 --> 18:09.970
Take a look!

412
18:12.650 --> 18:15.030
Look carefully at the enemy's deployment!

413
18:15.030 --> 18:16.340
Once the fighting starts,

414
18:16.340 --> 18:18.870
our tens of thousands of battle-weary troops

415
18:19.020 --> 18:20.740
will have to resist,

416
18:21.210 --> 18:22.440
from every direction at once,

417
18:22.440 --> 18:25.610
the pincer blows and infiltration thrusts of an enemy army hundreds of thousands strong.

418
18:25.610 --> 18:27.780
To cover the Central and Military Commission Columns,

419
18:27.780 --> 18:29.470
and the follow-up troops crossing the river,

420
18:29.470 --> 18:30.970
the 1st and 3rd Red Army Corps will fight

421
18:30.970 --> 18:33.380
in terrain unfit for holding actions,

422
18:33.820 --> 18:37.450
facing waves of assaults from enemies several times their number.

423
18:37.450 --> 18:38.500
For them,

424
18:38.740 --> 18:41.500
that means enormous, needless sacrifice!

425
18:42.130 --> 18:43.130
And what about us?

426
18:43.170 --> 18:45.060
We Central and Military Commission Columns

427
18:45.060 --> 18:46.860
are hauling heavy pots and pans,

428
18:47.130 --> 18:49.450
so we can cover only 20-odd li a day.

429
18:49.930 --> 18:51.450
Crossing the river in 2 days?

430
18:51.450 --> 18:52.450
Not a chance!

431
18:52.970 --> 18:56.210
Let alone the 8th and 9th Red Army Corps 200 li away.

432
18:56.610 --> 18:57.740
At this rate,

433
18:58.370 --> 18:59.890
our entire Red Army

434
19:00.130 --> 19:03.280
will be hemmed in on both banks of the Xiang River.

435
19:04.200 --> 19:06.730
We wouldn't be able to fly even if we had wings.

436
19:06.970 --> 19:07.780
Mao,

437
19:08.260 --> 19:13.860
stop raising alarmist talk.

438
19:13.860 --> 19:18.610
The bravery and tenacity of the Red Army are beyond question.

439
19:18.650 --> 19:19.450
That's the alarmist talk.

440
19:18.710 --> 19:19.820
[Wu Xiuquan, Translator]

441
19:19.450 --> 19:20.710
Don't translate that!

442
19:20.740 --> 19:21.600
That tone of his

443
19:22.130 --> 19:23.260
sounds familiar.

444
19:23.450 --> 19:24.970
It's nothing but the same phrases

445
19:24.970 --> 19:26.300
we always heard in the Central Soviet Area.

446
19:26.300 --> 19:29.410
And what was the result? We lost both the people and the land!

447
19:29.410 --> 19:31.410
We lost both the people and the land!

448
19:34.130 --> 19:35.130
My comrade,

449
19:35.450 --> 19:37.430
the bravery and tenacity of the Red Army

450
19:37.430 --> 19:39.100
must not be spent in needless sacrifice,

451
19:39.100 --> 19:41.820
and they must not become an excuse for our blind command!

452
19:41.820 --> 19:43.060
My comrade,

453
19:43.450 --> 19:44.820
how can you say the Central Committee

454
19:44.820 --> 19:46.300
is commanding blindly?

455
19:46.580 --> 19:49.540
This is the strategic direction approved by the Communist International,

456
19:49.540 --> 19:52.200
and the final decision of the supreme "Troika."

457
19:52.210 --> 19:54.370
No one has the right to change it blindly.

458
19:54.370 --> 19:55.890
I am still the Chairman of the Executive Committee

459
19:55.890 --> 19:57.220
of the Soviet Republic.

460
19:57.300 --> 19:59.500
If the main force of the Red Army is lost,

461
19:59.690 --> 20:00.860
what will be left?

462
20:01.370 --> 20:03.890
How is the Chinese revolution to go on?

463
20:05.110 --> 20:06.200
I believe

464
20:06.820 --> 20:09.780
victory lies in the final perseverance

465
20:10.260 --> 20:11.690
of the heroic Red Army.

466
20:12.210 --> 20:14.500
You may leave now.

467
20:49.940 --> 20:50.850
Comrades,

468
20:52.100 --> 20:54.690
this little town of Wenshi:

469
20:55.100 --> 20:56.760
east to west, it's one street,

470
20:57.890 --> 21:00.260
and north to south, it's one river.

471
21:01.020 --> 21:03.890
It's just like a cross.

472
21:04.450 --> 21:08.300
Right now, we are standing at this crossroads.

473
21:08.650 --> 21:11.690
Either we march toward destruction,

474
21:11.890 --> 21:12.720
or

475
21:14.370 --> 21:16.230
we march toward rebirth.

476
21:38.410 --> 21:40.690
Comrades Li De and Bo Gu,

477
21:41.130 --> 21:42.500
shouldn't we listen seriously

478
21:42.500 --> 21:46.260
to what Comrade Zedong just said?

479
21:46.330 --> 21:47.370
Comrade Bo Gu,

480
21:47.650 --> 21:48.970
Enlai is the General Political Commissar,

481
21:48.970 --> 21:50.830
and I am the Commander-in-Chief.

482
21:51.300 --> 21:52.890
We both suggest

483
21:52.970 --> 21:55.610
that you carefully and seriously

484
21:55.740 --> 22:00.060
consider Mao's opinion.

485
22:04.300 --> 22:06.700
Major strategic decisions can only be made

486
22:07.650 --> 22:08.890
by the "Troika."

487
22:15.370 --> 22:16.970
According to the deployment,

488
22:16.970 --> 22:18.540
the main force of the 1st Red Army Corps

489
22:18.540 --> 22:20.740
took up positions at Jiaoshanpu

490
22:21.000 --> 22:24.060
to block the Hunan Army advancing south from Quanzhou.

491
22:24.540 --> 22:26.380
The 4th Division of the 3rd Red Army Corps

492
22:26.380 --> 22:29.380
took up positions at Guanghuapu, south of Jieshou,

493
22:29.540 --> 22:32.450
to block the Guangxi Army from the direction of Xing'an.

494
22:32.450 --> 22:36.210
The 5th Division took up positions at Xinxu on the east bank of the Xiang River

495
22:36.210 --> 22:39.410
to block the Guangxi Army advancing north from Guanyang,

496
22:39.580 --> 22:43.100
ensuring the safety of the Red Army's corridor to the Xiang River.

497
22:43.100 --> 22:46.500
The 5th Red Army Corps held the line of Jiangjialing, Yong'an Pass,

498
22:46.500 --> 22:47.740
and Leikou Pass,

499
22:48.060 --> 22:50.370
covering the passage of the 8th and 9th Red Army Corps

500
22:50.370 --> 22:53.260
and holding back the pursuing KMT troops.

501
22:54.080 --> 22:55.600
[Jieshou Ferry, Xiang River, Guangxi]

502
22:54.920 --> 22:55.680
Hurry!

503
22:56.300 --> 22:57.610
Comrades, hurry!

504
22:56.430 --> 22:59.580
[Yang Yong, Political Commissar of the 10th Regiment, 4th Division, 3rd Red Army Corps]

505
22:57.780 --> 22:58.890
The comrades of the 1st Red Army Corps

506
22:58.890 --> 22:59.770
are waiting for our support!

507
22:59.770 --> 23:02.080
Hurry up. Hurry up.

508
23:03.340 --> 23:04.260
Hurry up.

509
23:06.820 --> 23:08.020
Comrades, hurry!

510
23:08.200 --> 23:09.370
The comrades of the 1st Red Army Corps

511
23:09.370 --> 23:10.970
are waiting for our support!

512
23:12.130 --> 23:13.330
Comrades, speed up!

513
23:17.290 --> 23:18.740
Grab two planks.

514
23:19.120 --> 23:19.780
Here, here, here.

515
23:19.780 --> 23:21.040
Come on, put them here.

516
23:23.120 --> 23:25.390
Battalion Commander! The engineer company of the Cadre Regiment has arrived!

517
23:25.390 --> 23:26.430
Battalion Commander Wang!

518
23:26.430 --> 23:27.070
Regiment Commander Chen!

519
23:27.070 --> 23:28.400
Come on. Good. Hurry.

520
23:29.170 --> 23:30.500
Battalion Commander Wang,

521
23:30.500 --> 23:32.690
do you have enough materials for the bridge?

522
23:32.690 --> 23:33.860
We brought some more.

523
23:33.860 --> 23:35.100
The local villagers have contributed plenty.

524
23:35.100 --> 23:36.300
Added to what you've brought, so that's more than enough.

525
23:36.300 --> 23:37.060
Good. Good.

526
23:37.690 --> 23:40.170
The Military Commission leaders say this pontoon bridge is especially important.

527
23:40.170 --> 23:41.580
The Central and Military Commission Columns

528
23:41.580 --> 23:42.690
and all the remaining troops

529
23:42.690 --> 23:43.930
will cross over it.

530
23:44.020 --> 23:45.640
Regiment Commander Chen, when will they get here?

531
23:45.640 --> 23:47.860
[Chen Geng, head of the Cadre Regiment of the 1st Military Commission Column]

532
23:48.170 --> 23:49.320
It's hard to say.

533
23:49.930 --> 23:51.100
But our orders are

534
23:51.300 --> 23:53.240
to keep this pontoon bridge open and clear.

535
23:53.240 --> 23:54.240
Once they arrive,

536
23:54.330 --> 23:55.970
we'll be ready to cross at any moment.

537
23:55.970 --> 23:56.740
Okay.

538
23:59.510 --> 24:03.660
[Guihuang Highway, Guangxi]

539
24:03.310 --> 24:06.070
Comrades, quick. Keep up!

540
24:16.080 --> 24:18.540
[Geng Biao, Commander of the 4th Regiment, 2nd Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

541
24:20.880 --> 24:23.210
Political Commissar, let me ask you something.

542
24:23.210 --> 24:24.210
Go ahead.

543
24:24.710 --> 24:25.350
Well,

544
24:25.080 --> 24:28.260
[Mao Zhenhua, Company Commander of the 3rd Company, 1st Battalion, 4th Regiment]

545
24:25.670 --> 24:27.890
is the whole army supposed to know that our 4th Regiment can run,

546
24:27.890 --> 24:28.780
or what?

547
24:28.860 --> 24:31.120
Why are all our missions forced marches?

548
24:31.500 --> 24:32.520
We'd barely taken Jieshou

549
24:32.520 --> 24:34.310
when we handed the position over to the 3rd Red Army Corps

550
24:34.310 --> 24:36.110
and were ordered to Jiaoshanpu.

551
24:36.370 --> 24:38.540
Running every single day is just not sustainable.

552
24:38.540 --> 24:39.450
Fewer complaints,

553
24:39.310 --> 24:42.310
[Yang Chengwu, Political Commissar of the 4th Regiment, 2nd Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

554
24:39.450 --> 24:40.250
more running.

555
24:42.430 --> 24:43.300
Quick!

556
24:43.330 --> 24:45.500
Geng! Geng!

557
24:48.690 --> 24:49.610
Geng?

558
24:50.370 --> 24:52.370
Geng, you can go onto the stretcher.

559
24:52.430 --> 24:53.260
No need.

560
24:55.370 --> 24:57.060
You're shaking with fever and still running so fast?

561
24:57.060 --> 24:58.790
Why won't you listen to reason?

562
24:59.760 --> 25:06.660
[Jiaoshanpu, Guangxi]

563
25:01.730 --> 25:02.200
Sun?

564
25:02.340 --> 25:02.700
Yes, sir.

565
25:02.700 --> 25:03.170
Give me some water!

566
25:03.170 --> 25:03.700
Yes, sir.

567
25:04.820 --> 25:05.650
Be careful.

568
25:13.420 --> 25:15.010
After the 4th Regiment rejoins its parent unit,

569
25:15.010 --> 25:16.740
our defense line at Jiaoshanpu

570
25:16.780 --> 25:18.130
will total four full regiments —

571
25:18.130 --> 25:19.590
the 2nd, 4th, 5th, and 6th.

572
25:19.870 --> 25:21.960
The front at Jiaoshanpu is too wide.

573
25:22.170 --> 25:24.740
Four regiments spread out won't look like enough.

574
25:24.740 --> 25:25.870
Telegraph Li Jukui:

575
25:26.410 --> 25:29.640
the other two regiments of the 1st Division

576
25:30.610 --> 25:31.020
Okay.

577
25:31.890 --> 25:34.150
Then where do we set up our headquarters?

578
25:35.420 --> 25:37.400
[Lin Biao, Commander of the 1st Red Army Corps]

579
25:36.570 --> 25:37.460
Right here.

580
25:37.400 --> 25:38.930
[Zuo Quan, Chief of Staff of the 1st Red Army Corps]

581
25:38.120 --> 25:39.720
I'll make the arrangements.

582
25:43.110 --> 25:45.900
We shouldn't have been here at all!

583
25:46.330 --> 25:50.150
[Nie Rongzhen, Political Commissar of the 1st Red Army Corps]

584
25:47.820 --> 25:49.280
Since we're already here,

585
25:49.300 --> 25:50.540
don't think about anything else.

586
25:50.540 --> 25:51.710
Right now, all we can hope for

587
25:51.710 --> 25:55.440
is that the Central and Military Commission Columns get here soon.

588
26:10.020 --> 26:16.510
[Jiangjialing, Yongzhou, Hunan, Headquarters of the 5th Red Army Corps]

589
26:10.370 --> 26:12.610
Collect the weapons and ammunition from the staff departments

590
26:12.610 --> 26:13.640
and distribute them to the combat units.

591
26:13.640 --> 26:14.360
Yes, sir!

592
26:20.550 --> 26:22.020
You made it here so quickly.

593
26:22.020 --> 26:23.350
Comrades Shuxiang and Cuilin,

594
26:23.350 --> 26:24.970
you've worked hard.

595
26:24.400 --> 26:25.990
[Liu Bocheng, Chief of Staff of the 5th Red Army Corps]

596
26:25.500 --> 26:26.410
The reason I called you here

597
26:26.410 --> 26:27.690
so urgently is that

598
26:27.720 --> 26:29.970
[Dong Zhentang, Commander of the 5th Red Army Corps]

599
26:27.890 --> 26:29.410
there is an extremely arduous task

600
26:29.410 --> 26:30.410
to hand to you two.

601
26:31.170 --> 26:31.780
Come here.

602
26:32.540 --> 26:34.300
At present, the Military Commission has issued

603
26:34.300 --> 26:36.430
the combat order to force a crossing of

604
26:36.580 --> 26:38.450
the Xiang River between Quanzhou and Xing'an.

605
26:38.450 --> 26:39.710
Our 5th Red Army Corps,

606
26:39.860 --> 26:41.260
as the army's rearguard,

607
26:41.370 --> 26:44.130
is ordered to hold the line of Jiangjialing, Yong'an Pass,

608
26:44.130 --> 26:45.300
and Leikou Pass.

609
26:45.410 --> 26:48.060
The Military Commission instructs the 34th Division to set out at once

610
26:47.930 --> 26:49.470
[Chen Shuxiang, Commander of the 34th Division, 5th Red Army Corps]

611
26:48.410 --> 26:50.450
for the Shuiche area of Guanyang.

612
26:49.470 --> 26:50.670
[Cheng Cuilin, Political Commissar of the 34th Division, 5th Red Army Corps]

613
26:51.020 --> 26:52.820
After covering the passage of the 8th and 9th Red Army Corps,

614
26:52.820 --> 26:54.580
you will then serve as the army's rearguard

615
26:54.580 --> 26:57.510
and cover all the troops in crossing the Xiang River.

616
26:58.780 --> 27:00.100
Come on, let's sit and talk here.

617
27:00.100 --> 27:00.530
Please, sit.

618
27:00.530 --> 27:01.120
Okay.

619
27:04.410 --> 27:05.570
This also means

620
27:06.060 --> 27:08.970
you will be the very last unit in the entire Central Red Army

621
27:08.970 --> 27:11.130
to cross the river.

622
27:11.780 --> 27:12.580
It is even...

623
27:15.260 --> 27:17.100
even possible that you may face the situation

624
27:17.100 --> 27:20.450
where your route is cut off by the enemy,

625
27:20.820 --> 27:24.080
unable to cross, fallen into the plight of fighting alone.

626
27:31.450 --> 27:32.650
Rest assured, Chief.

627
27:32.780 --> 27:35.210
The 34th Division guarantees it will accomplish the mission.

628
27:35.210 --> 27:36.470
Guaranteed, and accomplished well.

629
27:36.470 --> 27:37.070
Okay.

630
27:42.820 --> 27:45.500
If... if we cannot cross the river,

631
27:46.160 --> 27:47.640
how should we act?

632
27:48.270 --> 27:49.500
The Military Commission instructs:

633
27:49.500 --> 27:50.690
if you cannot cross,

634
27:51.060 --> 27:53.450
return to Hunan and wage guerrilla warfare.

635
27:53.450 --> 27:54.210
Understood.

636
27:54.410 --> 27:56.580
Comrades Shuxiang and Cuilin,

637
27:56.780 --> 27:59.540
most of the men of the 34th Division are from western Fujian,

638
27:59.540 --> 28:02.610
and many of its core cadres are veterans of the original 4th Red Army.

639
28:02.610 --> 28:04.650
It is a force that dares to fight hard battles

640
28:04.650 --> 28:06.210
and knows how to win them.

641
28:06.410 --> 28:08.300
Commander-in-Chief Zhu and Chairman Mao

642
28:08.300 --> 28:10.100
hold deep feelings for you.

643
28:10.300 --> 28:11.740
Please tell the Commander-in-Chief Zhu

644
28:11.740 --> 28:12.970
that we will certainly accomplish the mission

645
28:12.970 --> 28:14.580
the Military Commission has given us.

646
28:14.580 --> 28:16.060
And please tell Chairman Mao:

647
28:16.060 --> 28:17.450
I, Chen Shuxiang,

648
28:17.740 --> 28:19.260
have followed him from the fields of my hometown in Changsha

649
28:19.260 --> 28:21.130
all the way up the Jinggang Mountain,

650
28:21.130 --> 28:23.930
and I will follow him in revolution to the very end.

651
28:24.690 --> 28:25.860
Keep those words,

652
28:26.500 --> 28:28.410
and say them to Chairman Mao yourself

653
28:28.410 --> 28:30.480
once you've accomplished the mission.

654
28:30.480 --> 28:31.020
Okay.

655
28:33.210 --> 28:35.010
How many rounds do you have left?

656
28:36.170 --> 28:37.150
Eight rounds.

657
28:50.330 --> 28:50.930
Take care.

658
29:06.190 --> 29:09.320
Report! Urgent telegram from the Military Commission.

659
29:15.500 --> 29:16.630
We're in a hard spot.

660
29:16.860 --> 29:18.540
The 1st and 3rd Red Army Corps have it even harder.

661
29:18.540 --> 29:20.400
Comrades Lin Biao and Peng Dehuai

662
29:20.430 --> 29:21.690
are holding the gap open on both banks of the Xiang River,

663
29:21.690 --> 29:23.300
waiting for us.

664
29:24.340 --> 29:26.970
When the brave meet on a desperate path, the bold win.

665
29:26.970 --> 29:30.130
The Xiang River situation has become a half-crossed crisis.

666
29:30.130 --> 29:32.660
We must break through as quickly as possible.

667
29:38.020 --> 29:45.030
[Xinxu, Guangxi, Blocking Position of the 5th Division, 3rd Red Army Corps]

668
30:56.250 --> 30:59.380
Salute, Army Corps Commander and Political Commissar!

669
31:00.860 --> 31:02.450
We've come to see you.

670
31:03.100 --> 31:06.100
Comrades, the Military Commission's order to you is:

671
31:06.190 --> 31:07.900
at all costs,

672
31:08.780 --> 31:11.010
resolutely hold the Xinxu blocking position

673
31:11.010 --> 31:11.940
for 2 to 4 days,

674
31:12.070 --> 31:16.200
[Peng Dehuai, Commander of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

675
31:12.960 --> 31:14.290
protecting the flank safety of the Central Column

676
31:14.290 --> 31:16.330
and the follow-up crossing troops.

677
31:16.780 --> 31:17.930
I want to stress that

678
31:18.500 --> 31:19.740
this timeframe

679
31:20.020 --> 31:21.750
is only an approximate figure.

680
31:23.130 --> 31:24.930
Your position is only 5 kms north

681
31:25.060 --> 31:27.650
of the Military Commission Column's

682
31:28.500 --> 31:29.890
main march route,

683
31:29.720 --> 31:32.560
[Li Tianyou, Commander of the 5th Division, 3rd Red Army Corps]

684
31:30.450 --> 31:31.790
and there's no natural terrain to hold.

685
31:31.790 --> 31:33.540
If your position is broken through,

686
31:32.740 --> 31:35.440
[Zhong Chibing, Political Commissar of the 5th Division, 3rd Red Army Corps]

687
31:33.860 --> 31:35.580
then the Central and Military Commission Columns

688
31:35.580 --> 31:37.370
and the follow-up crossing troops

689
31:37.370 --> 31:39.450
will be in danger of being cut in half.

690
31:41.340 --> 31:45.340
Before the Military Commission decided to send the 5th Division to Xinxu,

691
31:45.340 --> 31:46.890
it consulted us.

692
31:46.680 --> 31:49.930
[Yang Shangkun, Political Commissar of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

693
31:47.540 --> 31:50.470
Many of the 5th Division's cadres, including you, Li Tianyou,

694
31:50.470 --> 31:52.240
had taken part in

695
31:52.270 --> 31:54.800
the Baise and Longzhou Uprisings in Guangxi.

696
31:54.860 --> 31:55.820
The Guangxi Army across from you

697
31:55.820 --> 31:57.170
is your old rival.

698
31:57.450 --> 31:59.710
You know their tactics relatively well.

699
31:59.890 --> 32:01.610
Now the two armies face each other again,

700
32:01.610 --> 32:04.500
and the result bears on the entire war situation.

701
32:04.970 --> 32:06.560
You must be mentally prepared

702
32:06.560 --> 32:08.620
for a decisive battle with the enemy.

703
32:08.920 --> 32:10.120
Rest assured, Chief.

704
32:11.060 --> 32:12.690
We'll hold

705
32:13.210 --> 32:14.890
as long as the higher-ups order us to hold.

706
32:14.890 --> 32:16.740
Until we receive the order to withdraw,

707
32:16.740 --> 32:19.200
the enemy won't set a single foot past Xinxu!

708
32:28.210 --> 32:30.530
Tianyou, if I remember correctly,

709
32:31.410 --> 32:32.670
you're 21, aren't you?

710
32:32.700 --> 32:33.750
One month shy.

711
32:35.330 --> 32:37.060
Zhong Chibing, what about you?

712
32:37.370 --> 32:38.430
We're the same age.

713
32:39.850 --> 32:41.250
A boy division commander

714
32:41.880 --> 32:43.610
and a boy political commissar.

715
32:43.610 --> 32:46.540
And also Hu Zhen, a veteran Red Army Chief of Staff.

716
32:47.890 --> 32:48.630
Good.

717
32:49.300 --> 32:50.450
From now on,

718
32:50.860 --> 32:51.930
your 5th Division

719
32:52.210 --> 32:55.100
will shoulder the heaviest burden in the entire army.

720
32:55.100 --> 32:57.130
You know it well.

721
32:57.540 --> 32:58.300
Yes, sir!

722
33:00.100 --> 33:01.210
Army Corps Commander,

723
33:01.210 --> 33:03.340
people say our names were well chosen.

724
33:03.340 --> 33:04.470
I'm called Tianyou,

725
33:04.890 --> 33:06.130
and he's called Chibing,

726
33:06.130 --> 33:07.460
which means "Red Army."

727
33:08.610 --> 33:10.010
When our names are put together,

728
33:10.010 --> 33:12.200
it will be "Heaven blesses the Red Army."

729
33:12.200 --> 33:13.800
Great!

730
33:15.520 --> 33:18.170
[Guilin, Guangxi]

731
33:15.890 --> 33:18.500
Vice Commander-in-Chief, an urgent telegram from the Chairman.

732
33:18.270 --> 33:22.380
[Bai Chongxi, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Guangxi Army]

733
33:25.740 --> 33:28.740
Generalissimo Chiang is getting anxious.

734
33:29.300 --> 33:30.160
What did he say?

735
33:31.600 --> 33:34.970
[Liu Fei, Senior Staff Officer of the Guangxi Army Headquarters]

736
33:35.590 --> 33:37.820
It seems there's no avoiding a fight now.

737
33:37.820 --> 33:39.300
I really can't fathom

738
33:39.300 --> 33:40.540
what the Communist leadership is thinking.

739
33:40.540 --> 33:42.020
Days ago, we opened up a corridor for them,

740
33:42.020 --> 33:43.100
and they wouldn't take it,

741
33:43.100 --> 33:46.100
dawdling along, marching straight to their own doom.

742
33:46.890 --> 33:48.130
Where do we strike?

743
33:50.020 --> 33:54.410
If we can't hit the tail, then we hit the waist —

744
33:55.260 --> 33:56.090
Xinxu.

745
33:58.230 --> 34:05.140
[Xinxu, Guangxi, Blocking Position of the 5th Division, 3rd Red Army Corps]

746
34:09.139 --> 34:10.320
Take cover!

747
34:10.370 --> 34:11.300
Take cover!

748
34:11.330 --> 34:11.989
Take cover!

749
34:12.139 --> 34:12.929
Take cover!

750
34:19.120 --> 34:20.159
Get down!

751
34:20.840 --> 34:22.219
Hug the trench wall!

752
34:22.409 --> 34:23.540
Hug the trench wall!

753
34:23.780 --> 34:25.010
Get down!

754
34:34.250 --> 34:36.960
On November 28, 1934,

755
34:37.739 --> 34:40.340
under the cover of aircraft and artillery fire,

756
34:40.340 --> 34:43.050
the KMT Guangxi Army's 44th Division

757
34:43.050 --> 34:44.050
launched wave after wave of furious attacks

758
34:44.050 --> 34:47.960
on our army's Xinxu position from Guanyang.

759
34:51.020 --> 34:56.969
[Jieshou Ferry, Xiang River, Guangxi]

760
35:17.010 --> 35:19.050
Comrades, repair the pontoon bridge!

761
35:19.050 --> 35:20.780
Comrades, follow me!

762
35:31.230 --> 35:33.350
Put out the fire!

763
35:33.740 --> 35:34.540
Put out the fire over here!

764
35:34.540 --> 35:37.060
Put out the fire! Hurry!

765
35:42.210 --> 35:47.320
[Jiaoshanpu, Guangxi, Position of the 1st Red Army Corps]

766
35:57.740 --> 35:58.800
Fire!

767
36:26.690 --> 36:30.980
[Jianfengling, Jiaoshanpu, Guangxi, Position of the 5th Regiment, 2nd Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

768
36:40.460 --> 36:42.940
Comrades, charge with me!

769
36:41.370 --> 36:44.230
[Yi Dangping, Political Commissar of the 5th Regiment, 2nd Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

770
36:43.710 --> 36:51.340
Attack!

771
36:53.050 --> 36:58.300
[Xinxu, Guangxi, Blocking Position of the 5th Division, 3rd Red Army Corps]

772
37:13.000 --> 37:19.430
[Jieshou Ferry, Xiang River, Guangxi]

773
37:13.780 --> 37:14.890
Hurry up.

774
37:14.890 --> 37:16.570
Okay. Come on.

775
37:17.260 --> 37:18.010
Take it.

776
37:20.260 --> 37:21.010
Hurry.

777
37:21.530 --> 37:22.570
To the left, left.

778
37:23.660 --> 37:24.410
Lift it up!

779
37:27.700 --> 37:28.450
Hurry up.

780
37:28.860 --> 37:29.620
Lift it up.

781
37:30.370 --> 37:30.930
Lift it up.

782
37:30.930 --> 37:31.700
Hold tight.

783
37:31.930 --> 37:32.790
Tie it tighter.

784
37:34.840 --> 37:35.600
Come on.

785
37:37.140 --> 37:37.930
Come on. Come on.

786
37:37.930 --> 37:38.680
Okay.

787
37:38.550 --> 37:43.300
[Jiaoshanpu, Guangxi, Position of the 1st Red Army Corps]

788
37:51.020 --> 37:57.760
[Jieshou Ferry, Xiang River, Guangxi]

789
38:59.860 --> 39:03.910
[Jiaoshanpu, Guangxi, Position of the 1st Red Army Corps]

790
39:01.370 --> 39:02.620
Move!

791
39:02.840 --> 39:04.400
Quick, go!

792
39:40.700 --> 39:42.370
On November 29,

793
39:42.740 --> 39:46.050
the battle erupted along the entire front on both banks of the Xiang River.

794
39:46.050 --> 39:48.050
The Hunan and the Guangxi Armies

795
39:48.050 --> 39:50.540
launched violent offensives, respectively,

796
39:50.540 --> 39:52.310
against the positions of the 1st and 3rd Red Army Corps

797
39:52.310 --> 39:54.490
holding the Jiaoshanpu and Guanghuapu lines.

798
39:54.490 --> 39:57.820
From the very first moment, the fighting reached a white heat.

799
39:57.820 --> 39:59.820
On every position, hopelessly outnumbered,

800
39:59.820 --> 40:02.130
the Red Army commanders and fighters

801
40:02.370 --> 40:04.570
fought the enemy desperately,

802
40:04.570 --> 40:05.890
hill by hill,

803
40:06.260 --> 40:08.190
beating back attack after attack.

804
40:08.370 --> 40:11.260
They paid a tremendous price in sacrifice to ensure

805
40:11.290 --> 40:14.280
the Military Commission Column's safe crossing of the river.

806
40:14.280 --> 40:15.570
Charge!

807
40:50.890 --> 40:56.270
[Jieshou Ferry, Xiang River, Guangxi]

808
41:56.460 --> 42:01.390
[Xinxu, Guangxi, Blocking Position of the 5th Division, 3rd Red Army Corps]

809
42:14.200 --> 42:18.140
[Guanghuapu, Guangxi, Position of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

810
42:29.340 --> 42:34.240
[Jiaoshanpu, Guangxi, Position of the 1st Red Army Corps]

811
42:39.050 --> 42:39.860
Kill them!

812
42:53.220 --> 42:58.140
[Guanghuapu, Guangxi, Position of the 3rd Red Army Corps]
